  "notes": "{腐敗|ふはい} can refer to either physical decay (rotting) or moral/political corruption.\n\nWRITING:\n- {腐|ふ} (rot, decay, spoil)\n- {敗|はい} (defeat, fail, deteriorate)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {腐敗|ふはい}する (to decay, to become corrupt - suru verb)\n- {腐敗|ふはい}した〜 (decayed ~, corrupt ~)\n\nSENSE 1 (Physical decay):\n- {腐敗|ふはい}{臭|しゅう} (smell of decay)\n- {腐敗|ふはい}{防止|ぼうし} (decay prevention)\n- {腐敗|ふはい}{菌|きん} (decay bacteria)\n\nSENSE 2 (Corruption):\n- {政治|せいじ}{腐敗|ふはい} (political corruption)\n- {腐敗|ふはい}{政治|せいじ} (corrupt politics)\n- {腐敗|ふはい}{体質|たいしつ} (corrupt nature/structure)\n- {腐敗|ふはい}した{官僚|かんりょう} (corrupt bureaucrats)\n\nPROVERB:\n- {権力|けんりょく}は{腐敗|ふはい}する (Power corrupts - from Lord Acton's dictum)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {堕落|だらく} (moral degradation)\n- {汚職|おしょく} (corruption - specifically bribery)\n- {腐|くさ}る (to rot - verb)\n- {衰退|すいたい} (decline, decay)",
